1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,580
This is what a sound looks like.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:08,900
One tone goes left, another goes right.
A beam draws where they meet.

3
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:14,050
Tune the second a little sharp,
and the shape turns.

4
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:17,210
That turning is the
beating the ear picks up.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,220
Slow it down. Closer.
Three to two, and it stops.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,710
A perfect fifth, held still.

7
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:29,950
Three touches across the top,
two down the side.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,900
Every simple ratio has its own shape.
An octave. A fourth. A major third.

9
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,350
Pull it out of ratio
and the shape tangles.

10
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,350
The ear calls that rough. So does the eye.

11
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:49,060
Every shape you saw was drawn by the
score. None was animated. It was played.
